  "Id": 2959,
  "Title": "Journey towards Gender Equity",
  "NewsSubTitle": null,
  "NewsSummary": "Implementation of Gender Equality, Inclusion and Diversity is necessary to attain the SDGs ",
  "GlobalNews": false,
  "AlternateNewsTitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSubtitle": null,
  "AlternateNewsSummary": null,
  "NewsContent": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Gender, Equality, Inclusion and Diversity (GEID), is crucial in teaching and educational practice. Experts say it is a necessity for the future of education as we strive towards attaining Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs)."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "These were some of the discussions at the GEID workshop hosted by the Aga Khan Universitys' Institute for Educational Development, East Africa (AKU-IED, EA). Over twenty faculty members from AKU-IED, EA and participants from the Madrasa Early Childhood Programme in Zanzibar (MECP-Z) were convened. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "\"Reaching the furthest behind first is the answer to leaving no one behind is a slogan that is advocated by most humanitarian organisations. This is what AKU-IED, EA can adapt in bridging the gap of GEID,\" said Dr Patrick Ojok, faculty at AKU-IED, EA."
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "In this case, GEID is about giving equal access and opportunities and removing the barriers of discrimination towards children, especially those who come from marginalized and vulnerable populations."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "The workshop was part of the "
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Foundations for Learning (F4L) Project",
            "marks": [
              {
                "type": "link",
                "attrs": {
                  "href": "https://www.aku.edu/iedea/Pages/f4ee.aspx",
                  "target": "_blank",
                  "linktype": "url",
                  "uuid": null,
                  "anchor": null,
                  "custom": {}
                }
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": " focusing on enhancing the agenda of GEID in the project intervention areas including: AKU-IED, EA's Master of Education programme; Teacher Education trainings for both pre-primary and primary education and Diploma in Educational, Leadership and Management programme. "
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "F4L mainly focuses on improving educational systems across East Africa at the pre-primary, primary and leadership levels to address gender, social cultural and economic barriers that women and girls face in accessing quality education."
          },
          {
            "type": "hard_break"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
